{
 "summary": "Checkout failures (gateway 5xx up to 76.5%) originate from slow responses in inventory POST /reserve, not from errors in it. Orders times out waiting on inventory and returns 504, which gateway surfaces as 502. Why inventory became slow is not shown: there are no deploy records, inventory logs or inventory dependency data in the snapshot.",
 "root_cause": {
  "statement": "Inventory POST /reserve (release 3.1.5) became slow starting about 10:29:59Z, with p95 rising to 4.8s while returning no 5xx. Orders calls to reserve inventory time out after about 2s, and orders returns 504, which gateway turns into 502 on POST /checkout. The underlying reason inventory slowed is not established by the evidence.",
  "service": "inventory",
  "confidence": "medium",
  "evidence_ids": [
   "ev-17b8e09b1a81",
   "ev-fd152cd71b58",
   "ev-e777a06fc951",
   "ev-9973be9a2c5e"
  ]
 },
 "contributing_factors": [
  {
   "statement": "Orders appears to time out calls to inventory at about 2s, below inventory's p95 of about 4.8s. As a result, orders fails most requests (5xx max 100%) instead of waiting for inventory to respond.",
   "evidence_ids": [
    "ev-fd152cd71b58",
    "ev-17b8e09b1a81",
    "ev-9f16798ba6ba",
    "ev-e777a06fc951"
   ]
  },
  {
   "statement": "Gateway turns every orders 504 into a 502 for checkout, so all 207 logged checkout failures map to orders timeouts.",
   "evidence_ids": [
    "ev-9973be9a2c5e",
    "ev-e777a06fc951",
    "ev-fd152cd71b58"
   ]
  }
 ],
 "timeline": [
  {
   "time": "2026-10-23T10:29:31Z",
   "event": "Orders begins logging 'timed out reserving inventory' and gateway begins logging 'checkout failed: orders returned 504' (207 occurrences each through 10:31:57Z).",
   "evidence_ids": [
    "ev-e777a06fc951",
    "ev-9973be9a2c5e"
   ]
  },
  {
   "time": "2026-10-23T10:29:59Z",
   "event": "Inventory p95 latency crosses 1s. Orders and gateway 5xx ratio crosses 5% and their p95 crosses 1s.",
   "evidence_ids": [
    "ev-17b8e09b1a81",
    "ev-9f16798ba6ba",
    "ev-a151ed13c014"
   ]
  },
  {
   "time": "2026-10-23T10:31:31Z",
   "event": "First sampled error trace in the pattern: gateway 502 <- orders 504, with dominant self time in inventory POST /reserve (release 3.1.5); 20 of 20 sampled traces match.",
   "evidence_ids": [
    "ev-fd152cd71b58"
   ]
  },
  {
   "time": "2026-10-23T10:31:57Z",
   "event": "Last observed timeout and checkout-failure logs. Gateway error ratio is still about 70% and orders 100% at the end of the window.",
   "evidence_ids": [
    "ev-e777a06fc951",
    "ev-9973be9a2c5e",
    "ev-a151ed13c014",
    "ev-9f16798ba6ba"
   ]
  }
 ],
 "ruled_out": [
  {
   "statement": "Inventory returning errors: its 5xx ratio is 0% throughout. The failure mode is latency, not inventory errors.",
   "evidence_ids": [
    "ev-17b8e09b1a81"
   ]
  },
  {
   "statement": "Gateway or orders as the origin: although both report errors, trace self time is dominated by inventory POST /reserve. Orders logs attribute the failures to inventory timeouts.",
   "evidence_ids": [
    "ev-fd152cd71b58",
    "ev-e777a06fc951"
   ]
  },
  {
   "statement": "A large traffic surge (weak evidence): gateway request rate stays modest at 1.98 rps on average and 2.36 rps at most, though no pre-incident baseline is available.",
   "evidence_ids": [
    "ev-a151ed13c014"
   ]
  }
 ],
 "unknowns": [
  "No deployment records are in the snapshot, so it is unknown whether inventory 3.1.5, or any other change, was rolled out shortly before 10:29Z.",
  "No inventory logs are present to explain why POST /reserve is slow (for example lock contention, a slow DB query, or exhausted pools).",
  "No metrics are available for inventory's downstream dependencies, such as a database or cache, or for its resource saturation.",
  "The exact orders-to-inventory timeout setting is unknown; about 2s is inferred from trace durations.",
  "No pre-incident baseline is available for latency or traffic."
 ],
 "recommended_actions": [
  {
   "action": "Check deploy history for inventory. If release 3.1.5, or a config change, went out shortly before 10:29Z, roll it back.",
   "rationale": "All failing traces show inventory 3.1.5 as the dominant self-time contributor. A recent change is the most common cause of a sudden latency step, but no deploy record is available to confirm this.",
   "evidence_ids": [
    "ev-fd152cd71b58",
    "ev-17b8e09b1a81"
   ]
  },
  {
   "action": "Inspect inventory POST /reserve directly: logs, traces of the example IDs (for example 4bed5353fc37dd4bcbd35cba261863f1), DB/lock metrics, CPU and connection pools.",
   "rationale": "Inventory is where the time is spent, yet it reports no errors, so the cause must be found inside or beneath inventory.",
   "evidence_ids": [
    "ev-fd152cd71b58",
    "ev-17b8e09b1a81"
   ]
  },
  {
   "action": "As a short-term mitigation, scale out inventory or shed load on /reserve. Consider whether orders should fail fast or circuit-break on inventory.",
   "rationale": "Inventory p95 of about 4.8s exceeds orders' roughly 2s timeout, which drives orders 5xx to 100%.",
   "evidence_ids": [
    "ev-17b8e09b1a81",
    "ev-9f16798ba6ba"
   ]
  }
 ]
}
